{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454817-2nd-edition-owod-how-to-create-a-horrifying-grappler-biter","id":1454817,"title":"[2nd Edition oWOD] How to create a horrifying grappler/biter?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-13T05:54:52-07:00","id":1454817,"title":"[2nd Edition oWOD] How to create a horrifying grappler/biter?","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> My idea for new character is a vampire who is absolutely terrifying when it comes to close quarter combat. Once he gets his hands on you - you are done. I don't want to abuse it, but I want others to fear my character reputation as absolute savage when it comes to fight and with that - my character has respect is harsh underground of gang-wars city.<br /> <br /> We play 2nd edition so no cost auto-success Potence is in play and 1 BP for full Celerity extra actions too. <br /> <br /> So I have few ideas:<br /> <br /> 1. Classic Brujah, start with 3 Potence, 1 Celerity + Maw merit. High DEX + WITs for Initiative. Action: Hold, Celerity 1 for Bite STR+2 Agg dmg, min.5 agg. For extra discipline at start I thought Fortitude<br /> 2. Lamia, Potence 3, Path of the Four Humours/Deimos 2 (Kiss of The Dark Mother). Maw Merit. High Dex + WITs. Action: Hold, next turn bite with Dark Mother Kiss for min of... 10 agg damage! That's enough to probably one-shot almost everything. For extra discipline at start I thought of Celerity, though it makes this character glass cannon...<br /> 3. I also though about Brujah but with added Serpentis 2 for Tongue + Celerity attacks and Serpentis 3 can be great replacement of Fortitude investment, however I really think Hold has huge merit instead of just attacking because it prevents enemy from doing anything else but trying to free himself. But I might be wrong and it's better than Hold-&gt;Bite combo.<br /> <br /> For merits I know Maw is the must for +1 extra damage from bite, Ability Apptitude (Brawl) is also great for that Hold and Bite attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","name":"Viben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T08:17:29-07:00","id":1454827,"title":"","content":"I probably wouldn't allow (3) right out the gate. The first two are legit, though. There are some prior threads here on the art of grapple/biting, so maybe they can offer some additional insights?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T08:44:28-07:00","id":1454830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454817-2nd-edition-owod-how-to-create-a-horrifying-grappler-biter?p=1454827#post1454827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably wouldn't allow (3) right out the gate. The first two are legit, though. There are some prior threads here on the art of grapple/biting, so maybe they can offer some additional insights?</div> </div> </div> </div>What's wrong with 3? I can buy Serpentis with Freebies.<br /> <br /> Also sadly Lamia is not available as I asked my STR so only Brujah + Serpentis or I could go Follower of Set Serpentis 3 at start and invest in Potence and Celerity 1 to level up later but that would be more xp costly than Brujah with Serpentis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","name":"Viben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T09:10:40-07:00","id":1454834,"title":"","content":"Nosferatu have a number of merits that are helpful for Grapples, though I am unsure if they go back to second edition. Stealth is really the best way to initiate grapples like a super predator, otherwise you end up just running at swords or gunfire. Animalism is also very good for grapplers since animals can take advantage of those you grapple and also because grappling works poorly when you're outnumbered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T09:42:47-07:00","id":1454838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Viben</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454817-2nd-edition-owod-how-to-create-a-horrifying-grappler-biter?p=1454830#post1454830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's wrong with 3? I can buy Serpentis with Freebies.<br /> <br /> Also sadly Lamia is not available as I asked my STR so only Brujah + Serpentis or I could go Follower of Set Serpentis 3 at start and invest in Potence and Celerity 1 to level up later but that would be more xp costly than Brujah with Serpentis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Serpentis is a relatively rare Discipline from an Independent Clan. Why would a Brujah have it? Maybe if you had a Setite mentor with the first step of a Blood Bond towards them, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T10:37:48-07:00","id":1454843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454817-2nd-edition-owod-how-to-create-a-horrifying-grappler-biter?p=1454834#post1454834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nosferatu have a number of merits that are helpful for Grapples, though I am unsure if they go back to second edition. Stealth is really the best way to initiate grapples like a super predator, otherwise you end up just running at swords or gunfire. Animalism is also very good for grapplers since animals can take advantage of those you grapple and also because grappling works poorly when you're outnumbered.</div> </div> </div> </div>What mertis you have in mind? I was thinking about Nosferatu but Animalism imo is not as useful as Presence and I would still have to buy Celerity. But Obsufscate is really nice, I just don't like how easy it is to counter it with Auspex automatically. Takes a lot from that Discipline consdiering how many clans have Auspex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","name":"Viben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T07:43:17-07:00","id":1454886,"title":"","content":"There was one for big hands or long fingers, another for extra nasty bite, and another that lets you slip out of grapples easier (slimy? Lizard limbs?) which might be really good when you find you've grappled more than you can chew. <br /> While Auspex is defo one of the -must have- disciplines that everyone should pick up eventually, usually you'll have more Obfuscate than they have Auspex, at least if it's an in-clan discipline, and I'm not sure about 2e rules specifically but the rules are pretty lopsided in favour of the stealthy character than the person looking for them in later editions. <br /> <br /> Animalism is severely underrated. Presence is powerful, but 1 is poorly worded in most editions and your ST may make it godly or shit. If you're using 2, you're not grappling, and using 3 is messy. 4 is nice and five is particularly interesting from the point of view of &quot;I'm grappling this guy, stay out of it&quot;.but at this point you're spending lots of XP on stuff that isn't grappling, and presence is both blood expensive and unreliable in comparison to Dominate and Animalism. Animalism 1/2 in contrast, are godly assists for the grappler. Grappling excells 1 vs 1, or 3 vs 2, but it's terrible when you're even slightly outnumbered, because you're really leaving yourself exposed while you've got two arms on a guy. Dogs are the most normal choice for fighting with animalism. If it's just you and a single dog, it can hamstring your single victim while you're grappling them, greatly increasing your odds. If it's you+dog vs two human opponents, the dog can take on one foe while you take care of another, or they can deter the second foe from getting involved in your 1v1 fight, or the dog can scare the shit out of both opponents and you simply need to run them down. If they've got a gun, the more-threatening dog can draw fire while you close the distance with your foe like a lunatic to grapple them. When you have animalism 2, you can call a horde of dogs. Animalism can do more at low levels and is more reliable than the high levels; it's generally not a good idea to Entrance a lot of people, because they get out of that and grow to hate you, but you can Feral whispers every dog in the neighbourhood to defend you whenever you call them with animalism 2. Other than dogs, there are more exotic/fun options for a grappler, like keeping a snake on your person to bite your foes when you've got them grappled, or you can hold people in place for the rat hordes to devour them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T17:41:53-07:00","id":1455001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454817-2nd-edition-owod-how-to-create-a-horrifying-grappler-biter?p=1454886#post1454886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was one for big hands or long fingers, another for extra nasty bite, and another that lets you slip out of grapples easier (slimy? Lizard limbs?) which might be really good when you find you've grappled more than you can chew.<br /> While Auspex is defo one of the -must have- disciplines that everyone should pick up eventually, usually you'll have more Obfuscate than they have Auspex, at least if it's an in-clan discipline, and I'm not sure about 2e rules specifically but the rules are pretty lopsided in favour of the stealthy character than the person looking for them in later editions.<br /> <br /> Animalism is severely underrated. Presence is powerful, but 1 is poorly worded in most editions and your ST may make it godly or shit. If you're using 2, you're not grappling, and using 3 is messy. 4 is nice and five is particularly interesting from the point of view of &quot;I'm grappling this guy, stay out of it&quot;.but at this point you're spending lots of XP on stuff that isn't grappling, and presence is both blood expensive and unreliable in comparison to Dominate and Animalism. Animalism 1/2 in contrast, are godly assists for the grappler. Grappling excells 1 vs 1, or 3 vs 2, but it's terrible when you're even slightly outnumbered, because you're really leaving yourself exposed while you've got two arms on a guy. Dogs are the most normal choice for fighting with animalism. If it's just you and a single dog, it can hamstring your single victim while you're grappling them, greatly increasing your odds. If it's you+dog vs two human opponents, the dog can take on one foe while you take care of another, or they can deter the second foe from getting involved in your 1v1 fight, or the dog can scare the shit out of both opponents and you simply need to run them down. If they've got a gun, the more-threatening dog can draw fire while you close the distance with your foe like a lunatic to grapple them. When you have animalism 2, you can call a horde of dogs. Animalism can do more at low levels and is more reliable than the high levels; it's generally not a good idea to Entrance a lot of people, because they get out of that and grow to hate you, but you can Feral whispers every dog in the neighbourhood to defend you whenever you call them with animalism 2. Other than dogs, there are more exotic/fun options for a grappler, like keeping a snake on your person to bite your foes when you've got them grappled, or you can hold people in place for the rat hordes to devour them</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I will look into Nosferatu too. Celerity 1 at start will cover Hold + Bite in same turn. This also gives me idea that with Obfuscate 4 and Celerity 2 I could Hold, Bite and then use Obfuscate 4 to dissapear and strike again next turn. Very terrifying scenario. Glass cannon build, but very effective hit'n'run killer.<br /> <br /> But I also got another interesting idea: Warrior Settite (strange I forgot about one as I one had a player with it). Potence, Serpentis and Presence. Serpentis 3 at start gives CC, no-grapple agg attacks (free burning wrath) and ability to soak all physical agg damage with Stamina at diff 5 and +1 to Bite damage. With Maw merity that is STR +3 Bite, STR tongue agg damage and 5-6 Stamina soak which is like Fortitude 5-6 for 1 point in Serpentis (for physical attacks obviously).<br /> <br /> Celerity 1 at start and it's pretty dam tanky and strong from right on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24341,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","user":"Viben","date":". 07-15-2021, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","name":"Viben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T00:14:47-07:00","id":1455013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Viben</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454817-2nd-edition-owod-how-to-create-a-horrifying-grappler-biter?p=1455001#post1455001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. I will look into Nosferatu too. Celerity 1 at start will cover Hold + Bite in same turn. This also gives me idea that with Obfuscate 4 and Celerity 2 I could Hold, Bite and then use Obfuscate 4 to dissapear and strike again next turn. Very terrifying scenario. Glass cannon build, but very effective hit'n'run killer.<br /> <br /> But I also got another interesting idea: Warrior Settite (strange I forgot about one as I one had a player with it). Potence, Serpentis and Presence. Serpentis 3 at start gives CC, no-grapple agg attacks (free burning wrath) and ability to soak all physical agg damage with Stamina at diff 5 and +1 to Bite damage. With Maw merity that is STR +3 Bite, STR tongue agg damage and 5-6 Stamina soak which is like Fortitude 5-6 for 1 point in Serpentis (for physical attacks obviously).<br /> <br /> Celerity 1 at start and it's pretty dam tanky and strong from right on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's legit. I would totally allow that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T14:13:56-07:00","id":1455041,"title":"","content":"Vicissitude and extra mouths in unexpected places?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T18:03:52-07:00","id":1455058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454817-2nd-edition-owod-how-to-create-a-horrifying-grappler-biter?p=1455041#post1455041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vicissitude and extra mouths in unexpected places?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lack on any tankiness or stealth and celerity and time needed to do that extra mounts (you can't just do them instantly when combat starts) eliminates Tzimitze as my pick.<br /> <br /> I started to look at everythng little more and it seems Nosferatu would be suprisingly great assassins. With High Obfuscate (3 pretty much negates the Appearance penalty), High Potence and even just 1-2 Celerity a Nosferatu with Feeding Tongue merit will be able to deal huge amount of agg damage with his tongue (3 points for 18 inches range) and kill target before it can react. 7th Gen + 4/5 Obfuscate at start and not many enemies will be able to ever see you becasue Auspex 5-6 is quite rare and even if they match you - it's still contested roll.<br /> <br /> The only thing I don't like about Obfuscate it's that it's paper&gt;scissors countered by Auspex....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","name":"Viben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-18T20:35:30-07:00","id":1455161,"title":"","content":"Nosferatu, take ECD Presence. If you absolutely, positively <i>must</i> go with the maw merit, it then serves double duty as it provides extra dice to Intimidation rolls. Otherwise, forget it (an extra damage die isn't that great) and take spawning pool instead. That way you get a virtually limitless supply of vermin ghouls and bonus dice to Animalism rolls, with all the non-combat benefits those entail (spies, messengers, et cetera) and can focus on a couple good attack dogs.<br /> <br /> ECD Presence seems an odd coupling with Nosferatu, but trust me, it works <i>fantastically</i>. As you don't have an Appearance rating, you don't have to spend valuable dots on it in character generation and can pump Charisma and Manipulation instead. Charisma being the key there, as it's the linked attribute for levels 2, 4, and 5.<br /> <br /> And don't forget, when using mask your effective Appearance becomes <i>two</i> which means you still get workable dice pools for Awe and Entrancement...this is precisely why that got nerfed in newer editions, and the vampire has to spend blood to get Appearance dots out of mask. Not that those are the valuable Presence levels for a Nosferatu. Dread Gaze, Summoning, and Majesty are the 900-pound gorillas in a Nosferatu's discipline arsenal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 07-18-2021, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}